{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310599,"nonce":"IjPGZuhTeQ6qeb1NJ6KO+bzmulo=","title":"FIXED 2026-09-05 — a method-level generic erases its params to I64, so the monomorphizer's TypeVar-matching inference never fired and ...","message":"**Mechanism.** `extract_generic_call` inferred a type argument only from a parameter declared\n`IrType::TypeVar(name)`. A method-level generic has none -- its parameters erase to I64 -- so every\ncall logged `cannot infer type_param 'T' ... SKIP specialization` (205 of them in one small case).\nThe template kept its `type_param_tag_fixups`, `references_type_params()` returned true, and\nCranelift installed `[trap-stub:generic]`; `test` and `main` then cascaded to stubs.\n\n**Fix, and why it must be a pair:**\n1. `extract_generic_call`: when no TypeVar param matches, and the callee has exactly ONE type param\n   and a non-empty `type_param_tag_fixups`, infer from the erased slots -- every I64-declared\n   parameter must have a concrete argument type (`inlining::concrete_arg_type`, now `pub(crate)`,\n   which sees through the erasure BitCast) and they must all AGREE. One slot known and another not\n   is NOT agreement: `eq(12, t.get())` over `T:(Float)` reads Int off the literal while the call\n   returns float bits, and the resulting tag compares them unequal.\n2. `rewrite_call_sites`: bitcast an F64 argument (and Cast+BitCast an F32) into any I64-declared\n   slot. **Inlining already did this** (`arg_coercions`, dee41319); a call that survives AS A CALL\n   had nobody to do it, and an f64 register in an integer slot is a register class Cranelift\n   refuses -- it PANICS `assertion left == right failed / left: Float right: Int` in\n   aarch64/inst/emit.rs, which surfaces as W0020 on the CALLER.\n\n**Landing step 1 alone LOSES 7 rows** (Issue12700/2835/3447/4000/6587/6942/7942 -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER or\nCRASH) for 2 gained. With step 2 the same build is 451 pass, 0 LOST, 12 GAINED.\n\n30s repro (needs TWO modules -- same-file `eq\u003cT\u003e` is inlined and never shows it):\n`$SP/eqrepro2/{Main.hx,unit/Test.hx}` -- `class Main extends unit.Test` calling\n`eq(123.e12, 123.E12)`. Insert coercions in DESCENDING instruction index so an insert never shifts a\nsite not yet rewritten. See [[project_generic_method_type_args_never_inferred.md]],\n[[bugs_conformance_scores_the_tiered_path_not_llvm.md]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_erased_generic_call_needs_a_bits_coercion` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}